            <ArticleTitle>Surgical treatment of coronary arteriovenous fistulas and aortic valve insufficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>380-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12102</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 76-year-old female with Takayasu arteritis who was found to have multiple coronary arteriovenous fistulas (CAVFs), a pulmonary-to-systemic ratio of 2:1, and aortic valve insufficiency. Aortic valve replacement and ligation of multiple CAVFs with cardiopulmonary bypass were performed under cardioplegic arrest, thus minimizing coronary steal.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2013 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
